# Next.js Performance Optimization Guide

## Overview
This skill covers key performance optimization techniques for Next.js applications, including API route optimization, bundle size reduction, and rendering efficiency.

## Key Topics

### 1. API Route Optimization

#### Parallel Requests
Instead of sequential API calls, use Promise.all() to fetch data in parallel:

```typescript
// SLOW - Sequential
const user = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/user`);
const products = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/products`);
const reviews = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/reviews`);

// FAST - Parallel
const [userRes, productsRes, reviewsRes] = await Promise.all([
  fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/user`),
  fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/products`),
  fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/reviews`)
]);
```

#### Batching API Calls
Combine multiple API calls into a single endpoint request to reduce network overhead:

```typescript
// Instead of 3 separate calls, make 1 call that returns all data
const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/products`);
const data = await response.json();
// Returns { user, products, reviews } in single request
```

#### Response Caching
Implement caching strategies to reduce redundant API calls:

```typescript
// In Next.js API routes, use fetch cache options
const response = await fetch(url, {
  next: { revalidate: 60 } // Cache for 60 seconds
});
```

### 2. React Component Optimization

#### Memoization
Use React.memo() to prevent unnecessary re-renders of child components:

```typescript
export const ProductCard = React.memo(({ product, onAddToCart }: Props) => {
  return <div>{/* component */}</div>;
}, (prevProps, nextProps) => {
  // Return true if props are equal (skip render)
  return JSON.stringify(prevProps) === JSON.stringify(nextProps);
});
```

#### useMemo Hook
Cache computed values to avoid recalculating on every render:

```typescript
const filteredProducts = useMemo(() => {
  return products.filter(p => p.name.includes(searchTerm));
}, [products, searchTerm]);
```

#### useCallback Hook
Memoize functions to maintain referential equality across renders:

```typescript
const handleAddToCart = useCallback((productId: string) => {
  setCartItems([...cartItems, productId]);
}, [cartItems]);
```

### 3. Bundle Size Reduction

#### Tree-Shaking and Selective Imports
Import only what you need from libraries:

```typescript
// SLOW - Imports entire library
import _ from 'lodash';

// FAST - Import specific functions
import { filter, map } from 'lodash';
```

#### Dynamic Imports
Load heavy libraries only when needed:

```typescript
// Load mathjs only when Compare page is rendered
const math = await import('mathjs');
```

#### Lightweight Alternatives
Replace heavy libraries with smaller alternatives:

- Use `lodash-es` instead of `lodash` for better tree-shaking
- Use native Array methods instead of Lodash for simple operations
- Consider lightweight alternatives to heavy math libraries

### 4. Next.js Specific Optimizations

#### Image Optimization
Use Next.js Image component for automatic optimization:

```typescript
import Image from 'next/image';

<Image
  src={productImage}
  alt="Product"
  width={200}
  height={200}
  placeholder="blur"
/>
```

#### Dynamic Imports for Code Splitting
Split code to load components only when needed:

```typescript
const HeavyComponent = dynamic(() => import('./HeavyComponent'), {
  loading: () => <p>Loading...</p>
});
```

#### force-dynamic Consideration
Evaluate whether `force-dynamic` is necessary. Use cached responses when possible:

```typescript
// Only use force-dynamic if data must be fresh on every request
// export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic';

// Prefer: Revalidate on a schedule instead
export const revalidate = 60; // Revalidate every 60 seconds
```

### 5. Performance Measurement

#### Web Vitals
Use Next.js web-vitals to measure core performance metrics:

```typescript
import { getCLS, getFID, getFCP, getLCP, getTTFB } from 'web-vitals';

getCLS(console.log);
getFID(console.log);
getFCP(console.log);
getLCP(console.log);
getTTFB(console.log);
```

#### Performance API
Use the browser's Performance API to measure specific operations:

```typescript
performance.mark('operation-start');
// ... perform operation
performance.mark('operation-end');
performance.measure('operation', 'operation-start', 'operation-end');
const measure = performance.getEntriesByName('operation')[0];
console.log(`Duration: ${measure.duration}ms`);
```

## Common Patterns

### Optimized Server Component Data Fetching

```typescript
async function HomePage() {
  // Fetch data in parallel
  const [userRes, productsRes, reviewsRes] = await Promise.all([
    fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/user`),
    fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/products`),
    fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/reviews`)
  ]);

  const [user, products, reviews] = await Promise.all([
    userRes.json(),
    productsRes.json(),
    reviewsRes.json()
  ]);

  return <HomePage user={user} products={products} reviews={reviews} />;
}
```

### Optimized Client Component with Memoization

```typescript
const ProductList = React.memo(({ products, reviews, onAddToCart }: Props) => {
  const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] = useState('');
  const [sortBy, setSortBy] = useState('name');

  // Memoize filtered/sorted products
  const filteredProducts = useMemo(() => {
    let result = products;
    if (searchTerm) {
      result = result.filter(p => p.name.toLowerCase().includes(searchTerm.toLowerCase()));
    }
    if (sortBy === 'price') {
      result = [...result].sort((a, b) => a.price - b.price);
    }
    return result;
  }, [products, searchTerm, sortBy]);

  return (
    <div>
      {filteredProducts.map(product => (
        <ProductCard key={product.id} product={product} onAddToCart={onAddToCart} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
});
```

## Tools for Analysis

- **Bundle Analyzer**: `@next/bundle-analyzer` - Visualize bundle size
- **Lighthouse**: Built-in performance auditing tool
- **Chrome DevTools**: Network and performance profiling
- **Next.js Speed Insights**: Monitor Web Vitals in production

## References
- Next.js Optimization Guide: https://nextjs.org/docs/app/building-your-application/optimizing
- React Optimization: https://react.dev/reference/react/memo
- Web Vitals: https://web.dev/vitals/

